<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 06:29:07 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump vows comeback as parties clash over Democrat prosecution threats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261109-trump-comeback-democrats-prosecution-threats</link><description>
President Donald Trump vowed a political comeback on Sunday after Republicans lost control of Congress in last Tuesday’s midterms, as incoming Democratic leaders pledged to hold his administration to account, and the attorney general promised to defend officials against threatened prosecutions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/796e5ff4-dafa-11f1-83cc-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/aa618a3631bceeecb3b6ee36d3cb0b937c9f5f89.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/796e5ff4-dafa-11f1-83cc-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/aa618a3631bceeecb3b6ee36d3cb0b937c9f5f89.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89efa1a6-dbd8-11f1-a76e-03031a2f4c21</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 01:13:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/796e5ff4-dafa-11f1-83cc-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/aa618a3631bceeecb3b6ee36d3cb0b937c9f5f89.jpg">© Alex Wroblewski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo criticises Milei’s austerity in Argentina, says growth must benefit all</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-argentina-visit-milei</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV arrived in Argentina on Sunday from Uruguay, where his Latin America tour began, facing calls to help bridge divisions after three years of austerity under President Javier Milei. The visit to Buenos Aires is the first by a pontiff to the late Pope Francis’s homeland in nearly four decades.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39bb378c-dbaf-11f1-8a96-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T200018Z-1909450093-RC2WJOAQHQ73-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-ARGENTINA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39bb378c-dbaf-11f1-8a96-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T200018Z-1909450093-RC2WJOAQHQ73-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-ARGENTINA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4209491c-dbc1-11f1-8d7e-cd9c7bda3277</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 22:23:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39bb378c-dbaf-11f1-8a96-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T200018Z-1909450093-RC2WJOAQHQ73-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-ARGENTINA.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Pope Leo in Latin America: Papal Politics and Peru</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261108-pope-leo-in-latin-america-papal-politics-and-peru</link><description>
Pope Leo heads to Argentina for the second leg of his South America tour, where he's expected to draw the biggest turnout of his Papacy so far. The pontiff has wrapped up his first visit to Uruguay. Colleen Dulle, Vatican Correspondent at America Magazine and the co-host of the 'Inside the Vatican' podcast, joins us to analyse the significance of his Latin American tour.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51ec3fd0-dbab-11f1-b6cb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/ColleenTN811.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51ec3fd0-dbab-11f1-b6cb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/ColleenTN811.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b628278a-dbb9-11f1-ac32-4364c774d43a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 21:16:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Alessandro XENOS</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope Leo in Latin America: Papal Politics and Peru</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-in-latin-america-papal-politics-and-peru</link><description>
Pope Leo heads to Argentina for the second leg of his South America tour, where he's expected to draw the biggest turnout of his Papacy so far. The pontiff has wrapped up his first visit to Uruguay. Colleen Dulle, Vatican Correspondent at America Magazine and the co-host of the 'Inside the Vatican' podcast, joins us to analyse the significance of his Latin America trip.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51ec3fd0-dbab-11f1-b6cb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/ColleenTN811.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51ec3fd0-dbab-11f1-b6cb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/ColleenTN811.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4afa2b5c-dbb4-11f1-8c13-1bf2a2dbf315</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 20:51:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo urges men to respect wives amid Latin American femicide crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-urges-husbands-to-respect-wives-amid-femicide-crisis-across-latin-america</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV urged men to respect their wives as he wrapped up the first leg of his 12-day tour of Latin America. The region recorded nearly 20,000 instances of women being killed over the past five years alone, most of them murdered by a current or former partner.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e848f45a-db7e-11f1-a13c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6fab64bab726aafee6cdce3d68af60d2c79255ea.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e848f45a-db7e-11f1-a13c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6fab64bab726aafee6cdce3d68af60d2c79255ea.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e95bad06-db7e-11f1-94ec-63ab1173e7a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:15:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e848f45a-db7e-11f1-a13c-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6fab64bab726aafee6cdce3d68af60d2c79255ea.jpg">© Rodrigo Arangua, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Paraguay: Senate impeached Peña rather than accept his offer to resign</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261108-paraguay-senate-impeached-pe%C3%B1a-rather-than-accept-his-offer-to-resign</link><description>
Paraguay's ousted president, Santiago Peña, has been charged over the collapse of Ueno Bank. Initially placed under house arrest, he has since been transferred to a military facility for his own safety. Nearly three million customers were locked out of their accounts after regulators seized control of the online bank. Repayments are now under way, but protests continue as customers demand access to their money. Peña denies any wrongdoing. Jack Pownall reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97992746-db60-11f1-b875-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111033-111218-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/97992746-db60-11f1-b875-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-111033-111218-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c89fc9e-db60-11f1-b55f-b7e2ef7616a9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:42:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump wants UFC fighters as assistants</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-wants-ufc-fighters-as-assistants</link><description>
After a series of combative press briefings between the Trump administration and journalists, the US president surprised many by reportedly offering Dana White, the head of the Ultimate Fighting Championship (UFC) and a longtime friend, the role of White House press secretary. Trump praised White as a “violent fighter and warrior”, but US media reports say he has already turned down the offer. Was it a punchy choice by the president or simply a punchline? Jack Pownall takes a closer look.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad7ce2ee-db58-11f1-b2b1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-101159-101400-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ad7ce2ee-db58-11f1-b2b1-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-101159-101400-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b289ad26-db58-11f1-ae95-2ff3ce4ecc5e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:44:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'A violent fighter and warrior': Trump offers press secretary role to UFC chief Dana White</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-a-violent-fighter-and-warrior-trump-offers-press-secretary-role-to-ufc-chief-dana-white</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Saturday said he was asking mixed martial arts promoter Dana White to be the new White House press secretary. Trump has repeatedly tried to hitch his MAGA brand of politics to White's enormously successful Ultimate Fighting Championship.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1699b72c-dadf-11f1-8689-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4336TP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1699b72c-dadf-11f1-8689-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4336TP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d329b48-dade-11f1-b828-3bf6f8d3d03e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 20:45:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1699b72c-dadf-11f1-8689-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4336TP.jpg">© Jim Watson, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Paraguay’s impeached president charged over business links to bank collapse</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-paraguay-s-impeached-president-charged-over-bank-collapse</link><description>
Paraguay’s impeached president Santiago Peña was on Saturday charged over his business links to a major online bank whose sudden collapse locked millions of people out of their money and sparked angry protests.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13a50202-db1f-11f1-b25a-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/1af5d113e86f17a56a0a0a89ac52628e81d81c00.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13a50202-db1f-11f1-b25a-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/1af5d113e86f17a56a0a0a89ac52628e81d81c00.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e005f3a4-dac2-11f1-b6bb-73dfdcf8e7c2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 15:49:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13a50202-db1f-11f1-b25a-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/1af5d113e86f17a56a0a0a89ac52628e81d81c00.jpg">© Daniel Duarte, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo calls on Uruguay's Catholics to be 'bridge builders'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-calls-on-uruguay-catholics-bridge-builders</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV urged Catholics in Uruguay to build bridges of faith and fraternity on the second day of his 12-day tour of Uruguay, Argentina and Peru. The pope's three-country tour comes just three weeks after he underwent surgery for lung cancer.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edae6460-dab7-11f1-9ce0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-07T142220Z-1810286401-RC22JOA4XV14-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edae6460-dab7-11f1-9ce0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-07T142220Z-1810286401-RC22JOA4XV14-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3b5a6236-dab8-11f1-a64e-555534403bc1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 14:59:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edae6460-dab7-11f1-9ce0-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-07T142220Z-1810286401-RC22JOA4XV14-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Banking scandal topples Paraguay leader</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/banking-scandal-topples-paraguay-leader</link><description>
Paraguay’s ousted president Santiago Peña has been placed under house arrest after senators unanimously voted to remove him over a banking scandal. The collapse of Ueno Bank left nearly three million customers unable to access their savings. Peña denies any wrongdoing, while his successor, Pedro Alliana, has pledged to compensate those affected.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d0782be-daa4-11f1-b656-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-121224-121408-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6d0782be-daa4-11f1-b656-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-121224-121408-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">728b63f4-daa4-11f1-a5cc-51c017d118d8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:16:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Stephen Miller named White House Chief of Staff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/stephen-miller-named-white-house-chief-of-staff</link><description>
Following historic Republican losses in the midterm elections, Donald Trump has replaced his chief of staff, Susie Wiles, with her deputy Stephen Miller, the architect of his administration’s immigration crackdown. Wiles had been seen by some as a stabilising force in the White House, but with Democrats now controlling both chambers of Congress, Trump is reportedly seeking a more aggressive approach to pushing his agenda. Caroline Baum reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4bca0edc-daa4-11f1-9347-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-120813-120953-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4bca0edc-daa4-11f1-9347-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-120813-120953-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">50d33980-daa4-11f1-8747-e129e10de091</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:14:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope urges healthcare for all in Uruguay</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pope-urges-healthcare-for-all-in-uruguay</link><description>
Three weeks after undergoing surgery for lung cancer, Pope Francis has begun a three-nation tour of Latin America, saying he felt better than he looked. His first stop is Uruguay, the continent’s most secular country. Jack Pownall reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b2ce00a4-da8e-11f1-a2d2-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-101157-101324-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b2ce00a4-da8e-11f1-a2d2-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-101157-101324-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8150620-da8e-11f1-801f-71870b021f26</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 09:41:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>USA: Democrats vow to investigate Donald Trump</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/usa-democrats-vow-to-investigate-donald-trump</link><description>
In this new era of divided government, Democratic lawmakers say their priorities will be tackling the rising cost of living, investigating alleged corruption and tightening oversight of ICE agents. Antonia Kerrigan reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fe04a50-da8e-11f1-9600-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-091022-091213-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fe04a50-da8e-11f1-9600-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-091022-091213-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">14ec2a78-da8e-11f1-bf00-1b13d614584b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 09:36:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Paraguay places ousted president Peña under house arrest after bank collapse</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-ousted-paraguay-president-under-house-arrest-after-banking-crisis</link><description>
Paraguayan authorities placed ousted president Santiago Peña under house arrest on Friday, shortly after the Senate unanimously removed him from office over a massive banking crisis that locked nearly half of Paraguayans out of their savings. Peña offered his resignation over the scandal, but lawmakers pressed ahead with impeachment proceedings that stripped him of political immunity.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80d2986c-da70-11f1-91a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26309755276700.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80d2986c-da70-11f1-91a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26309755276700.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a6016c44-da70-11f1-927e-531e5467269d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 06:18:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/80d2986c-da70-11f1-91a8-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26309755276700.jpg">© Laura Fioravanti, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Giant pandas loaned by China make their public debut at US zoo</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-giant-pandas-loaned-by-china-make-public-debut-at-us-zoo</link><description>
Zoo-goers watched two giant pandas loaned by China make their public debut Friday in Atlanta, where they will be hosted for the next 10 years. The pair joins the many pandas shipped to zoos around the world as part of Beijing's "panda diplomacy" program aimed at cultivating foreign ties.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b123314-da55-11f1-b136-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6954e253f59dc1167792579db119c5a354d40d3c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b123314-da55-11f1-b136-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6954e253f59dc1167792579db119c5a354d40d3c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5c119016-da55-11f1-9c89-67661bde8add</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 02:45:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b123314-da55-11f1-b136-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/6954e253f59dc1167792579db119c5a354d40d3c.jpg">© Elijah Nouvelage, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo calls for healthcare to be 'accessible for all' during Uruguay visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-pope-leo-arrives-in-uruguay-for-first-stop-on-12-day-south-america-tour</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV on Friday called for healthcare to be "accessible to all" as he began a visit to Uruguay just three weeks after having undergone lung surgery. The 12-day tour of South America, which will also include stops in Argentina and Peru, is seen as something of a homecoming for the pontiff, who lived in Peru for almost two decades and holds joint US and Peruvian citizenship.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aab0508-da1a-11f1-81c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-06T193927Z-1437835472-RC2JIOACA4EZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aab0508-da1a-11f1-81c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-06T193927Z-1437835472-RC2JIOACA4EZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3283e0f4-da24-11f1-a6d8-95d5f1845f91</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 21:14:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0aab0508-da1a-11f1-81c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-06T193927Z-1437835472-RC2JIOACA4EZ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-URUGUAY.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump announces immigration hardliner Stephen Miller as new chief of staff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-announces-immigration-hardliner-stephen-miller-as-new-chief-of-staff</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Friday said advisor Stephen Miller would become his new chief of staff. Miller has been instrumental in driving the Trump administration's mass deportation programme and faced particular criticism after the deadly shootings of two Minneapolis protesters by ICE agents in January.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4ccbd52-da20-11f1-92bf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6PN3T3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4ccbd52-da20-11f1-92bf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6PN3T3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac163ece-da21-11f1-a81a-0383cf3d852d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 20:51:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e4ccbd52-da20-11f1-92bf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6PN3T3.jpg">© Chip Somodevilla, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title>Midterms: A Maga PostMortem, Europe’s ‘Shape Shifting’ Protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261106-midterms-a-maga-postmortem-europe-s-shape-shifting-protests</link><description>
A World This Week ‘Mid Terms Special’ 
 
Gavin Lee is joined by panel of four distinguished international correspondents to assess the aftermath of the worst Republican election result since the 1970s, post Watergate. We ask, is peak MAGA over? What will now change at home and abroad? And who ends the week in pole position as Presidential frontrunner for 2028?
 
We also consider the scale and scope of Europe Wide Protests:  
 
This week housing organisations, trade unions and activist groups from seven countries met in Paris issuing a joint call for demonstrations. Are the national protest movements becoming a coordinated European movement?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e82e01f4-da1b-11f1-b402-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/81f9ea5b-a81b-4236-b01d-3d25e74ea1f6.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e82e01f4-da1b-11f1-b402-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/81f9ea5b-a81b-4236-b01d-3d25e74ea1f6.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7761de0-da1d-11f1-8391-1b8f54bdb46f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 20:08:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Alessandro XENOS</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>A homegrown Georgia moderate and pragmatist: Is Senator Ossoff the future of the Democratic Party?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-a-homegrown-georgia-moderate-and-pragmatist-is-senator-ossoff-the-future-of-the-democratic-party</link><description>
Is Senator Jon Ossoff the future of the Democratic Party? Following a resounding midterm victory in Georgia, a former Republican stronghold, the 39-year-old senator has emerged as a prominent figure as the Democrats look ahead to 2028 for their next presidential nominee. His natural confidence, polished media performances and ability to appeal to a diverse electorate have prompted comparisons with Barack Obama. Yet behind the excitement surrounding his national prospects lies a more complicated question: whether political momentum in the Senate necessarily translates into a presidential frontrunner.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b07c7ea8-da0b-11f1-ba8e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-181104-182336-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b07c7ea8-da0b-11f1-ba8e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261106-181104-182336-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2bf03f84-da1b-11f1-b582-41f7c3676cec</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 19:49:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>US midterms mark 'the beginning of the end' for Trump, John Bolton says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261106-us-midterms-mark-the-beginning-of-the-end-for-trump-john-bolton-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, John Bolton, who served as national security adviser to Donald Trump during his first term, called the US midterm results "the beginning of the end" for Trump's stranglehold on the Republican Party. Democrats regained control of both the House of Representatives and the Senate earlier this week, marking the Republicans' worst performance since the 1974 elections in the wake of the Watergate scandal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/329cac82-da02-11f1-8c02-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-john-bolton.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/329cac82-da02-11f1-8c02-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-john-bolton.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce3e0d66-d9f8-11f1-8676-4f5175760546</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 17:26:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope Leo embarks on Latin America trip with a first stop in Uruguay</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-pope-leo-embarks-on-latin-america-trip-with-a-first-stop-in-uruguay</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV is kicking off a three-nation tour of Latin America on Friday, November 6, with a visit to Uruguay, the region’s least Catholic and most secular country, three weeks after undergoing lung cancer surgery that had put the entire trip into question. After Uruguay, he will then go to Argentina and Peru. FRANCE 24's Hanna Roberts has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1dde444-d9ec-11f1-875a-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15e9c5b9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1dde444-d9ec-11f1-875a-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15e9c5b9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5bee38e6-d9ec-11f1-b58a-d3ec7f982f66</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 14:58:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>California governor to grant clemency to all 548 death row inmates in state</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-california-governor-to-grant-clemency-to-all-548-death-row-inmates-in-state</link><description>
California's governor Gavy Newsom announced Thursday that he will commute all death sentences in the state to life without the possibility of parole. He said that "capital punishment is morally wrong." The state Supreme Court will have the final say in hundreds of those cases.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06d29b9a-d9ec-11f1-b5f2-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-77fd1be3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06d29b9a-d9ec-11f1-b5f2-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-77fd1be3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7555a644-d9eb-11f1-b34b-9de4add3b6a8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 14:54:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>The women who rode the blue wave</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261106-the-women-who-rode-the-blue-wave</link><description>
In this edition, we report on how the US midterms, which saw the Democrats make massive gains, also marked a series of historic firsts for women. Also the dark side to Bangkok's booming fertility industry, which attracts thousands of foreign patients seeking assistance from the Thai capital's state-of-the-art private clinics. Plus how an impoverished neighbourhood in El Salvador, once a no-go zone plagued by gang violence, is being transformed by women into a vibrant canvas for street art.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f4db7a4-d9d7-11f1-b5a5-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f4db7a4-d9d7-11f1-b5a5-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7cd75936-d922-11f1-86b5-ef0b033d2e60</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 14:15:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump’s stillborn diesel deal: Why Russian oil tankers are not heading to the US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261106-trump-stillborn-diesel-deal-why-russian-oil-tankers-are-not-heading-to-the-us</link><description>
The first oil tankers scheduled to deliver Russian diesel to the US under a deal between President Donald Trump and his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin have changed course and are no longer heading toward the US coast. It spells the end of an agreement announced with great fanfare before the midterms.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/583fe45e-d93a-11f1-9d4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/image-tanker-diesel3.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/583fe45e-d93a-11f1-9d4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/image-tanker-diesel3.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72572b5c-d9d7-11f1-aa8a-15a9cc0740e7</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:38:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/583fe45e-d93a-11f1-9d4e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/image-tanker-diesel3.png">© Studio graphique France Médias Monde</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's future in question after midterms setback</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-us-defence-secretary-pete-hegseth-s-future-in-question-after-midterms-setback</link><description>
US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth's future is in question after Tuesday's, November 3, midterms setback. On Thursday, November 5, he issued a video message vowing to fight efforts in Congress to impeach him and defending the ‌Iran war as “courageous and historic”. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/786ab9d8-d9d6-11f1-88c5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bcc8d7a2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/786ab9d8-d9d6-11f1-88c5-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bcc8d7a2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee8dbbc0-d9d5-11f1-bdf5-e56d28bb9ded</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:15:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tech giants lose $1 trillion in one day after Democrats' victory in midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-tech-giants-lose-1-trillion-in-one-day-after-democrats-victory-in-midterms</link><description>
Vast sums have been wiped off the stock value of major tech firms in the US, Europe and Asia. Investors appear worried about the possibility of an AI slowdown and tougher regulation after Democrats won the midterms in the US. Some of the Democratic candidates had expressed their opposition to the data centres that are needed to power AI technology.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e1d77ee-d9dc-11f1-9d72-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f9220cf.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e1d77ee-d9dc-11f1-9d72-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4f9220cf.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d57022c-d9dc-11f1-817e-cfc74dac3b1b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:15:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Canada PM Mark Carney unveils budget to strengthen economy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-canada-pm-mark-carney-unveils-budget-to-strengthen-economy</link><description>
Canada's Prime Minister Mark Carney unveiled his first ever budget on November 5, which set out strong ambitions for greater economic independence from the US. The "Masters of our Destiny" budget also announced generous measures for parts of the economy affected by tariffs, setting aside 44 billion Canadian dollars for impacted businesses and workers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56f49bae-d9de-11f1-9e2c-cd4b49fae717</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:10:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Will Democratic Party introduce a new 'New Deal'? Key narrative must be 'focused on economic issues'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/will-democratic-party-introduce-a-new-new-deal-key-narrative-must-be-focused-on-economic-issues</link><description>
With Democrats poised to control both chambers of Congress, the party faces a defining challenge: how to constrain Donald Trump's presidency while carving out a path to the White House in 2028. For Ian Reifowitz, Distinguished Professor of History at SUNY Empire State University, the answer lies in drawing on the historical legacy of Franklin D. Roosevelt's New Deal coalition. Republicans, he argues, have progressively shifted electoral competition towards questions of identity, immigration and cultural conflict. Democrats, by contrast, must recover their traditional strength on economic security, affordability and everyday living standards. "These Democrats across the country ran on affordability." And that's how they must govern, explains Reifowitz.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d72ef50a-d9dc-11f1-96ab-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261105-223101-224205-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d72ef50a-d9dc-11f1-96ab-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261105-223101-224205-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dc7309f2-d9dc-11f1-ba9c-9776752ee81a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:07:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Period of uncertainty: Trump is tormented, he's unstoppable, and he's desperate for immortality'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261106-period-of-uncertainty-trump-is-tormented-he-s-unstoppable-and-he-s-desperate-for-immortality</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Craig Copetas, Greek-American author, international affairs columnist and editor at Türkiye Today and French Senator Hélène Conway-Mouret. "What you have is a tormented and unstable president who's desperate for immortality." With this arresting assessment, Copetas captures what he considers the defining paradox of Donald Trump's presidency in the aftermath of the US midterm elections: a leader politically neutered at home but potentially emboldened on the international stage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87cc9f50-da11-11f1-9afb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-abe726d1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87cc9f50-da11-11f1-9afb-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-abe726d1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0cb298f0-d9e0-11f1-ae27-6156df5d338f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 12:46:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
